  data: {
    LLM: "Players take turns adding tiles to either end of a single line, matching ends. Doubles are played across the line. If you cannot play, draw from the boneyard until you play a tile or the boneyard is reduced to two tiles (the last two are never drawn); with only two left and no play, pass. Hand ends when one player dominoes or the layout is blocked. Lowest pips in hand wins the hand; winner scores sum of losers' pips minus own total; tie for lowest scores nothing.",
    Player: "Players take turns adding tiles to either end of a single line, matching ends. Doubles are played across the line. If you cannot play, draw from the boneyard until you play a tile or the boneyard is reduced to two tiles (the last two are never drawn); with only two left and no play, pass. Hand ends when one player dominoes or the layout is blocked. Lowest pips in hand wins the hand; winner scores sum of losers' pips minus own total; tie for lowest scores nothing.",
    objective: 'Empty your hand first by matching tile ends to the line, or have the fewest pips when the game is blocked. Draw from the boneyard when you cannot play. Game is played to 100 points (2P/partnership) or 61 (3–4P).',
    gameplay: "Players take turns adding tiles to either end of a single line, matching ends. Doubles are played across the line. If you cannot play, draw from the boneyard until you play a tile or the boneyard is reduced to two tiles (the last two are never drawn); with only two left and no play, pass. Hand ends when one player dominoes or the layout is blocked. Lowest pips in hand wins the hand; winner scores sum of losers' pips minus own total; tie for lowest scores nothing.",
    keyRules: [
      'Match tile ends to either end of the line; doubles played across.',
      'Draw from boneyard when unable to play until you can play or boneyard has two tiles.',
      'Last two boneyard tiles are never drawn; if blocked with two left, pass.',
      'Hand ends at first domino or when blocked; lowest pips wins hand; first to 100 (or 61 in 3–4P) wins game.',
